<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 113,841 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 113,841 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 113,841 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday, compared to 63,366 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Monday	   Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			 9,989	    1,884</p>
<p>    Import cargo		     103,852	   61,482</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours six ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	   Tonnes/TEUs   Ship	   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	   67,281	 Johar	   18/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel 56,000	 Konpolis	22/10</p>
<p>High speed deisel 52,000	 Al Maqwa	19/10</p>
<p>Palm oil	    12,000	 Wawasan Megah 22/10</p>
<p>Soybean oil	 11,500	 Red Azelea    21/10</p>
<p>Sulphur		5,000	 Calimenesti   23/10</p>
<p>Gas oil	     28,000	 Fair Seas     18/10</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
